# Wave W17-U (Route 202): city post — a city-approach post flanking the path where the beds thicken: a squared post carrying two pale bands and a flat civic cap, the city’s own furniture reaching out to meet the road (design: Revelry’s lights are on in daylight; its posts stand dressed before its doors). On gate turf (fully opaque, ground baked in) — split from Route 201’s mile posts by the twin bands and cap: the mile post measures distance, the city post announces arrival.
